(a) the central assistance provided to Karnataka under the Silk Samagra Scheme and for handloom and powerloom development during each of the last three years;
(b) share of Karnataka in the national raw-silk production;
(c) the proposals from Karnataka pending with the Ministry; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen the sericulture and handloom sectors in the State?

(a) the status of implementation of Labour Codes and the reasons for delay, if any; 
(b) the latest estimate of unemployment rate, as per the Periodic Labour Force Survey; 
(c) the number of gig and platform workers registered on e-Shram portal and the social-security benefits extended to them; and 
(d) the steps taken for creation of employment?

(a) the Central funds allocated and released to Karnataka under the Development Action Plan for Scheduled Castes during each of the last three years;
(b) the funds released under the Post-Matric Scholarship for Scheduled Caste students in Karnataka and any amount pending;
(c) the reasons for shortfall or delay, if any; and
(d) the steps taken to release the pending funds?

(a) the Central assistance provided to Karnataka for computerisation of Primary Agricultural Credit Societies, and the number of societies covered; 
(b) the Central schemes of the Ministry under which Karnataka's cooperative institutions have received assistance during the last three years; 
(c) the proposals from Karnataka pending with the Ministry; and 
(d) the steps taken to strengthen the cooperative sector in the State?

(a) the amount of GST compensation released to Karnataka up to the end of the compensation period and any amount that remains pending;
(b) the estimated annual revenue shortfall to Karnataka following cessation of GST compensation;
(c) whether any successor mechanism to protect the States' revenues is under consideration; and
(d) the steps taken to address the resulting fiscal stress on the States?

(a) whether the Sixteenth Finance Commission has commented on or recommended rationalisation of unconditional cash-transfer or welfare schemes of the State Governments; 
(b) if so, the details and the action-taken response of Government;
(c) whether any conditionality relating to such State schemes is proposed to be attached to central transfers; and 
(d) the mechanism, if any, through which Government monitors or reviews such welfare schemes of the States?

(a) the Central share due to Karnataka under the Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) and the amount released and pending as on date;
(b) the reasons for delay in release of the pending Central share;
(c) the revised timeline for achieving full functional household tap connections in the State of Karnataka; and
(d) whether any policy for retrofitting and augmentation of completed works has been approved?

(a) the status of appraisal and approval of the irrigation projects submitted by the State of Karnataka in February, 2025 for the Central assistance under PMKSY-AIBP and FMBAP;
(b) the Central assistance sanctioned, if any;
(c) whether the Upper Krishna Project Stage-III has been considered for declaration as a National Project; and
(d) the timelines for according approvals?

(a) the central funds allocated and utilised for conservation and development of centrally-protected monuments in Karnataka, including the World Heritage Sites of Hampi and Pattadakal, during each of the last three years; 
(b) the number of proposals received from the State for protection or development of monuments pending with the Central Government; 
(c) the reasons for pendency, if any; and 
(d) the steps taken to conserve and promote State's heritage sites?

(a) Central funds allocated and released under Saksham Anganwadi and Poshan 2.0 during each of the last three years, State-Wise and whether any amount is pending, details thereof; 
(b) the number of Anganwadi centres in Karnataka sanctioned for upgradation and the assistance provided; 
(c) the reasons for shortfall or delay in release, if any; and 
(d) the steps taken to strengthen child nutrition and Anganwadi services in the State of Karnataka?

(a) the amount of the health component of the Health and Education Cess credited to the Pradhan Mantri Swasthya Suraksha Nidhi (PMSSN) during each of the last three years; 
(b) whether any portion of the collected health cess was retained in the Consolidated Fund of India instead of being transferred, as observed by the Comptroller and Auditor General; 
(c) the utilisation of the Nidhi for health infrastructure; and 
(d) the corrective steps taken?

(a) the number of street vendors who have received loans and paid back in full, under the PM Street Vendor's AtmaNirbhar Nidhi (PM SVANidhi) scheme since its launch and the total amount disbursed and received back, State-wise;
(b) the number of vendors who availed subsequent, higher loan tranches;
(c) whether any assessment of the socio-economic condition of urban street vendors has been undertaken; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen their livelihoods and social security?

(a) the central equity share committed and released for Phase 3 of the Bengaluru metro rail project as on date;
(b) the present status of the Central Government's approval and funding decision for the proposed Phase 3A (Red Line) corridor;
(c) the reasons for delay, if any, in according such approval; and
(d) the steps taken to expedite central support for the Bengaluru metro network?

(a) the present status of the Bengaluru Suburban Rail Project, corridor-wise and the revised date of completion;
(b) the reasons for revision of the completion deadline of the project;
(c) the total sanctioned cost of the project, the Central share therein and the funds released and utilised so far; and
(d) the steps taken to expedite completion of the project?

(a) the present status of implementation of the National Sports Governance Act, 2025, including the constitution of the National Sports Board and the National Sports Tribunal;
(b) whether the rules under the Act have been notified and if not, the timeline therefor;
(c) the manner in which the Act is proposed to ensure accountability, transparency and good governance in National Sports Federations; and
(d) the steps taken to bring National Sports Federations and the BCCI into compliance with the Act?

(a) the present status of the Bengaluru Satellite Town Ring Road (STRR) project, including approvals pending with Government;
(b) whether the project has been cleared by the Public Private Partnership Appraisal Committee and the further steps required for its commencement;
(c) the length of National Highways sanctioned in Karnataka and the funds released in the last three years; and
(d) the details of major National Highway projects in Karnataka pending clearance or funding?

(a) the amount collected through cesses and surcharges in each of the last three financial years and their share in the gross tax revenue of the Union;
(b) whether such cesses and surcharges do not form part of the divisible pool of taxes shared with the States;
(c) whether Government has received representations from State Governments regarding the rising share of cesses and surcharges; and
(d) the response of Government thereto?

(a) the grants recommended for rural local bodies in Karnataka under the 15th Finance Commission for the years 2024-25 and 2025-26;
(b) whether an amount of about ?2,860 crore in such grants for Gram Panchayats in Karnataka is pending release, if so, the reasons therefor;
(c) the tied and untied grants actually released to Karnataka's rural local bodies in each of the last three years; and
(d) the timeline for release of the pending grants?

(a) the latest assessment of the housing shortage in urban areas of the country;
(b) the total number of houses sanctioned and completed under Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana–Urban (PMAY-U) 2.0 as on date and the central assistance released against them;
(c) whether there is a gap between the assessed shortage and the houses sanctioned so far and if so, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the measures being taken to bridge this gap within the mission period?

(a) whether the Central Government announced central assistance of ?5,300 crore for the Upper Bhadra Project in Karnataka in the Union Budget 2023-24, and the amount released so far, year-wise;
(b) the present status of according National Project status to the upper Bhadra project, and the reasons for the delay in releasing the committed assistance;
(c) whether the Central Government is aware that the project is intended to provide irrigation and drinking water to the drought-prone districts of central Karnataka; and
(d) the timeline by when the balance assistance will be released?

(a) whether Government of Karnataka has sought a special central grant for urban infrastructure in Bengaluru and the details and present status thereof;
(b) the number of houses sanctioned and the central assistance released to Karnataka under Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana–Urban (PMAY-U) 2.0 since its launch;
(c) whether any proposals from Karnataka under the scheme are pending with the Central Government and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken to expedite release of Central funds to the State?

(a) the reasons for the consistent underutilization of funds allocated for the modernisation and strengthening of the Directorate General of Quality Assurance (DGQA); 
(b) the manner in which this impacts its ability to perform its critical mandate;
(c) whether Government will ensure that the reduced budgetary allocations in the current fiscal year do not adversely affect the smooth functioning and capacity building of the DGQA; and
(d) the steps Government is taking to ensure optimal and uniform utilisation of funds for DGQA throughout the financial year, rather than surrendering unspent amounts at the end?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government has announced in 2015 the setting up of a National University of Disability Studies and Rehabilitation Sciences;
(b) if so, the details reasons for the delay in setting up of this university;
(c) whether Government has prepared any roadmap along with clearly defined timelines for expeditiously enabling the university to become operational; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether it is a fact that a large number of sanctioned houses under PMAY(U) remain incomplete with the deadline fast approaching;
(b) Government's strategy to ensure their completion;
(c) the reasons for the underutilization of funds under this critical scheme, and the measures the Ministry is taking to ensure that States generate demand and absorb the allocated central assistance; and
(d) whether Government will direct States to converge other Central and State schemes, such as the PM Surya Ghar Muft Bijli Yojana, with PMAY (U) to provide basic amenities and ensure the timely occupancy of completed houses?

(a) the reasons for slow progress of doubling and quadrupling of key railway lines in Karnataka;
(b) the year-wise breakdown of physical progress and funds allocated versus actual expenditure of doubling and quadrupling of key railway lines for these projects over the last three years;
(c) whether Detailed Project Reports (DPRs) for quadrupling the lines to Mysuru, Tumakuru and Jolarpettai from Bengaluru have been submitted to Railway Board;
(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;
(e) the specific reasons for slow progress in the Yeshwanthpur-Channasandra and Baiyappanahalli-Hosur doubling projects; and
(f) their new completion dates?
