(a) whether the Ministry has formally examined the long-standing demand to create a unified railway zone for coastal Karnataka with its headquarters in Mangaluru, if so, the steps taken in this regard and the reason for the delay in taking a decision;
(b) whether Government is aware that this administrative fragmentation is directly responsible for the region's stunted railway development; and
(c) the steps Ministry is taking to accelerate pending railway projects in the Mangaluru and Karwar sections?

(a) the current vacancy count for Group-I scientist positions at the Council of Scientific & Industrial Research (CSIR);
(b) the overall vacancy rate within CSIR;
(c) factors which are contributing to these vacancies; and
(d) the timeline for filling these critical scientific and technical positions in a mission-mode approach to prevent further erosion of our premier research institution and how does this crisis of human capital signify for India's scientific ambitions?

(a) the vacancies in the post of teacher in the Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan (KVS); 
(b) the vacancies in the post of teacher in the Navodaya Vidyalaya Samiti (NVS); 
(c) the vacancies in the post of Group 'A' academic posts in the National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT); 
(d) the vacancies in the National Council for Teacher Education (NCTE); and 
(e) vacancy rate for non-teaching/ non-academic staff in these institutions?

(a) whether coconut farmers of Karnataka are facing problems because the price of copra have fallen from ?14,500 to ?9,400 per quintal, considering the fact that coconut cultivation has grown in Karnataka over the last 20 years;
(b) if so, whether Government is aware of this steep fall in price of copra; and
(c) the manner in which Government proposes to support coconut farmers?

(a) whether Government is aware that the annual Kodava family hockey tournament, hosted this year, has made history by earning itself a reference in the Guinness World Records for being the largest field hockey tournament;
(b) whether Government has taken a note of this event; and
(c) the financial assistance that has been offered or will be provided to this event?

(a) whether Government is aware of hardships of commuters and vehicle owners face on national highways due to excessive toll tax;
(b) the amount NHAI collects from users of expressway between Bengaluru and Mysore, whether road users find the cost of travel exorbitant; and
(c) whether NHAI has received any feedback, if so, the details of action proposed to reduce the cost of travel?

(a) whether the Progressive River Authority for Water and Harmony (PRAWAH) has conducted an inspection of the project sites of the riparian States of Goa, Maharashtra and Karnataka in July 2024;
(b) the legal ambit of the powers of PRAWAH; 
(c) whether PRAWAH has noted the abysmal condition of Karnataka with regard to drinking water difficulties in and around the twin cities of Hubli-Dharwad; and
(d) whether PRAWAH is bound by the report of the Mahadayi Water Disputes Tribunal (MWDT) passed by a high-ranking tribunal headed by a sitting Judge of the Supreme Court of India under Art 262 of the Constitution of India?

(a) the number of students, appearing and passing Class 10th and Class 12th CBSE Board Exams from schools in NCT of Delhi, the details for last five years, separately for Class 10th and Class 12th;
(b) the number of these students, appearing and passing the Class 10th and Class 12th CBSE Board Exams from (a) Private Schools, (b) Delhi Government Schools, (c) Central Government and Army/ Police Schools and (d) Delhi Government Aided Schools, details of last five years, separately for Class 10th and Class 12th; and
(c) the reason for rise in number of students in private schools?

(a) the targeted requirement (in litres/capita/day) of water supply, suggested by the CPHEEO for Metropolitan Cities with piped water supply where a sewerage system exists is contemplated;
(b) the quantity of water (in litres/capita/day) the Delhi Jal Board (DJB) distributes in NCT of Delhi;
(c) the reasons for the NCT of Delhi facing water shortage if the amount of water treated and distributed is within the per capita norm;
(d) the details of tankers deployed by DJB since 2019; and
(e) the norms for water released by Haryana to Delhi, month-wise list of total water allocated and released to Delhi from Haryana in last five years?

(a) whether it is a fact that in 2021, the Niti Aayog released a 'National Monetization Pipeline', which was supposed to serve as an essential roadmap for the asset monetisation of various brownfield infrastructure assets across different sectors;
(b) the target laid down for this roadmap in terms of raising finance and physical targets for various sectors;
(c) whether Government has met the set targets under the 'National Monetization Pipeline'; and
(d) the future plans to achieve set targets under this National Monetization Pipeline?

(a) the details of year-wise break-up of each of the 4 components (since the inception of the scheme), i.e., PMAY-U has four components: in-situ rehabilitation of existing slum dwellers, credit-linked subsidy scheme (CLSS) for EWS, affordable housing in partnership (AHP), and subsidy for beneficiary-led individual house construction, in terms of allocation by the Ministry, resources transferred by the Ministry, number of houses sanctioned and number of houses completed under the scheme;
(b) the State-wise list of existing houses demolished/grounded, but not completed, along with the period since grounded; and
(c) the reasons for the above?
